// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 5. VOLATILITY METRIC
//    Normalised ATR expressed as a 0–100 percentage of price.
//    Thresholds used: <30 = Stable, <80 = Moderate, else Volatile.
//    Returns: float (0–100)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
f_getVolatilityMetric() =>
    _raw   = ta.atr(14) / close * 100   // ATR as % of price
    // Scale so typical equity/crypto ranges map to 0–100
    // Raw values ~0–4% become 0–100 after ×25 cap at 100
    math.min(_raw * 25, 100.0)

